{"title":"POST/TABLE shared keys (official article)","input_uri":"/post/TABLE","methods":["POST"],"evidence":"shared","product_hint":"Official article narration is primarily CIVIL NX; treat as shared convention, not a Gen runtime test.","official_url":"https://support.midasuser.com/hc/en-us/articles/45171987915929-Designing-with-Intent-The-Vision-Behind-POST-TABLE","edited":"2026-07-30","fields":[{"key":"TABLE_TYPE","name":"Result table type","type":"String","required":"Required"},{"key":"TABLE_NAME","name":"Response title","type":"String","required":"Optional"},{"key":"EXPORT_PATH","name":"Save JSON path","type":"String","required":"Optional","notes":"Handbook paths like C:\\MIDAS\\... are placeholders."},{"key":"UNIT","name":"Output unit object","type":"Object","required":"Optional","notes":"FORCE, DIST, HEAT, and TEMP (not TEMPER) in this article."},{"key":"FORCE","name":"Force unit","type":"String","required":"Optional","group":"UNIT","enums":["N","KN","KGF","TONF","LBF","KIPS"]},{"key":"DIST","name":"Length unit","type":"String","required":"Optional","group":"UNIT","enums":["M","CM","MM","FT","IN"]},{"key":"HEAT","name":"Heat unit","type":"String","required":"Optional","group":"UNIT","enums":["CAL","KCAL","J","KJ","BTU"]},{"key":"TEMP","name":"Temperature unit in post/TABLE UNIT","type":"String","required":"Optional","group":"UNIT","enums":["C","F"],"notes":"Different from /db/UNIT TEMPER."},{"key":"STYLES","name":"Format/place styles","type":"Object","required":"Optional"},{"key":"COMPONENTS","name":"Result components","type":"Array","required":"Optional"},{"key":"NODE_ELEMS","name":"Node or element selection","type":"Object","required":"Optional","notes":"KEYS, TO, or STRUCTURE_GROUP_NAME (choose one)."},{"key":"PARTS","name":"Element parts","type":"Array/String","required":"Optional","notes":"Used by some tables."},{"key":"LOAD_CASE_NAMES","name":"Load case names","type":"Array","required":"Optional"}],"notes":"FIBER_CELL_MINMAX, SECT_POSITION, OUTPUT_STEP were described as JP fiber-section time-history keys; do not treat as default Civil or Gen capability.","keywords":["TABLE","结果","结果表"]}
{"title":"NX series JSON conventions (official online manual introduction)","input_uri":"","methods":[],"evidence":"shared","official_url":"https://support.midasuser.com/hc/en-us/articles/33016922742937-MIDAS-API-Online-Manual","edited":"2026-07-14","notes":"Manual introduction states it covers the MIDAS NX series, including CIVIL NX and GEN NX. That is not the same as every listed endpoint being verified on both products. /doc/* is POST only and the body starts with Argument; empty Argument may be {}. /db/* POST/PUT start with Assign then numeric keys; unique data such as Unit uses key \"1\". SAVE only saves the current file and is not a backup. SAVEAS switches the current file.","fields":[{"key":"Argument","name":"Document endpoint body key","type":"object/string","group":"/doc"},{"key":"Assign","name":"DB write first key","type":"object","group":"/db POST/PUT"}],"keywords":["文档","约定"]}
